Examples
========

Build the extension first (from the distribution root):

    perl Makefile.PL
    make

Use gmake instead of make with Strawberry Perl on Windows.
Then run any example, for example:

    perl eg/tabs-drag.pl

The scripts locate the distribution's lib and blib directories themselves,
so they also work when launched by absolute path from another directory.
A graphical desktop is required.

  tabs-drag.pl             IDE layout with draggable source-code tabs
  capture-release.pl       Release a frame into a window and capture it again
  drag-shadow.pl           Display and hide a drag outline inside a frame
  drag-shadow-toplevel.pl  Drag an outline around the desktop with the mouse

lib/testTextEdit.pl supplies source-code text widgets for examples and GUI tests.
The tab demo uses only this distribution's dependencies; no instrument-control
modules or measurement hardware are needed.
